flowchart TB
  s1["1. The planner records a rule<br/>Scenarios page, CLI or POST /scenarios/{id}/edits: an area,<br/>a feature type, an attribute and a value, stored as a row of<br/>curated_geo.scenario_edit under an app_core.scenario"]
  s2["2. Recompute materialises the rules<br/>POST /scenarios/{id}/recompute or the CLI scenario recompute:<br/>materialize_scenario resolves each rule into per-feature rows of<br/>curated_geo.scenario_override, refusing values above a ceiling"]
  s3["3. A scenario asset version is published<br/>so that freshness resolution sees the edit"]
  s4["4. The impact engine resolves the dirty set<br/>Only the indicators that read an edited attribute,<br/>plus every indicator that depends on them"]
  s5["5. A run is submitted and executed<br/>Deduplicated by a content fingerprint, enqueued on the DBOS<br/>runs queue; the worker takes units from the units queue<br/>in dependency waves, checkpointing each"]
  s6["6. Each unit computes over effective values<br/>override, then observation, then the base attribute;<br/>results are new indicator_result rows carrying the scenario_id"]
  s7["7. The client compares by scenario<br/>GET /scenarios/{id}/comparison; an indicator the scenario<br/>did not recompute falls back to its baseline value"]

  s1 --> s2 --> s3 --> s4 --> s5 --> s6 --> s7

  classDef step fill:#f2f5f9,stroke:#5d82a8,color:#000
  class s1,s2,s3,s4,s5,s6,s7 step
